; A "filter sweep" on FM: the modulator's TL sets how bright the note is, so a
; curve on it opens and closes the sound. Inline, a curve is a timeline sweep
; across notes; in a (macro ...) it restarts at every key-on. A looping curve
; inline is an auto-wah: a sin on an eighth-note clock locks the wah to the
; tempo (:dr3 0 stops the voice's own pluck there, so the wah is the only
; filter). One sweep over two bars, a snap on every note, then the wah.
(import "presets/waveforms/set.mmlisp")

(def riff c c > c < c c > c < c c e- c > c < c c g c)

(fm1 :tempo 128 :oct 2 :len 16 acid-saw
  :tl3 (ease-inout-sine 60..10 :len 2/1) (x 2 riff)      ; one sweep, two bars
  (macro :tl3 (ease-out-expo 10..60 :len 8)) (x 2 riff)  ; every note snaps open
  (macro none) :dr3 0 :tl3 (sin 12..56 :len 8) (x 2 riff)) ; an eighth-note wah
